    "result_text": "The suite contains a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full run is green: **2 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a typed getter/setter.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ...)` and an `ownerSegment(Owner)` method that composes `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n- **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` \u2014 reusing the existing banded membership-level logic.\n- **AREA** = `METRO` when `locality(owner)` is a known region (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`), else `REGIONAL` \u2014 reusing the existing locality derivation, so `UNKNOWN` correctly maps to `REGIONAL`.\n\nThis matched the two acceptance tests: a known-region owner at level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and an unknown-city owner \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
